I wrote the review to `docs/hoplite/c5_d084_rev2_2026-11-07/review_SONNET.md`. That file is the only change in the working tree. I synced to origin/main HEAD `e8b6367c1bd16b010318145587aaaedc14a77027`, where `git pull --ff-only` reported "Already up to date".

I read the full request, the rev2 draft and the prior synthesis, plus the audit code, the audit JSON, the v1 extractor and the per-checkpoint eval files. The source data (`data/external/*.jsonl`) is not in the repo. So I could not re-run the audit or read the source text of specific documents. I ran only in-memory checks on committed files:
- v1 extractor probes on synthetic strings;
- a paired bootstrap on per-document F1;
- Clopper-Pearson (CP) arithmetic.

I did not open test 163, use P1, run any model, or propose any gate change.

